Well, I explain. Imagine that we have 1 Finnish server and 6 American
ones. Alice is in Finland and Bob is in America, and for some reason they
have bad connectivity to each other's countries.

Now Bob has only a small advantage in the whole tournament, in that one
American server can be down and he can continue to play, whereas Alice has
to stop if the Finnish server is down.

But Bob has an *enormous* advantage in doing a hat trick with bells on. He
can just play humans on server A, elves on server B, etc. and stop each
one when he has a character of the appropriate race on the correct altar
with the Amulet; he gets his bells effectively for free, in that they're
no more work for him than doing the hat trick. Conversely Alice has to
ascend five games in a row - a much more difficult task.

>I can see how you could say it diminishes the achievement a bit, but we've
>always figured that was outweighed by the benefit of a player being able to
>switch to playing on another server if one has a problem.

That only matters if that server remains inaccessible to that player (but
not generally - if a server just dies obviously you wouldn't count games
started there but not finished) for the rest of the tournament.
